o a cost that could not be represented traps here rather than wrapping);"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"4(n + 1)(the greatest |cost| of a non-loop edge + 1) fits in "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the solver’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"artificial cost, with room for its potentials and reduced costs; computed in "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never reported); the positive supplies sum within "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"name":"Precondition","style":"note","type":"aside"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"A least-cost flow meeting every supply (positive: the vertex sends that much more than it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receives; negative: a demand), within capacities (LEMON ","type":"text"},{"code":"NetworkSimplex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", OR-Tools","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SimpleMinCostFlow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"code":"min_cost_flow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the opposite sign), or nil when there is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"none: the supplies do not sum to zero, or some set of vertices supplies more than its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out-edges carry. Costs may be negative; negative cycles are saturated (capacities are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"finite). A self-loop carries its capacity when its cost is negative and nothing otherwise.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Network simplex with block-search pivots and strongly feasible trees, LEMON’s layout.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"supply","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called once per vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"verti